Terminology {#terminology}
==========================

The key words "MUST", "MUST NOT", "REQUIRED", "SHALL", "SHALL NOT", "SHOULD", "SHOULD NOT", "RECOMMENDED", "NOT RECOMMENDED", "MAY", and "OPTIONAL" in this document are to be interpreted as described in BCP 14 [[!RFC2119]] [[!RFC8174]] when, and only when, they appear in all capitals, as shown here.

All of the text of this specification is normative except sections explicitly marked as non-normative, examples, and notes.

Examples in this specification are introduced with the words "for example" or are set apart from the normative text with <code>class="example"</code>, like this:

<div class="example" id="example-example"><a class="self-link" href="#example-example"></a>This is an example of an informative example.</div>

Informative notes begin with the word "Note" and are set apart from the normative text with <code>class="note"</code>, like this:

NOTE: This is an example of an informative note.

Bitstream features overview {#bitstream-overview}
=================================================

An [=AV2 bitstream=] is composed of a sequence of [=OBUs=] (Open Bitstream Units), grouped into [=Temporal Units=]. A Temporal Unit consists of a [=Temporal Delimiter OBU=] and all following OBUs up to, but not including, the next Temporal Delimiter OBU. Each Temporal Unit is associated with a single presentation time.

Every OBU begins with a 1- or 2-byte header that carries the [=obu_type=] and the temporal layer identifier [=obu_tlayer_id=]. When the OBU header extension is present (i.e. when [=obu_header_extension_flag=] is equal to 1 in that header), two additional layer identifiers are carried: the embedded layer identifier [=obu_mlayer_id=] and the extended layer identifier [=obu_xlayer_id=]. Depending on its type, an OBU can carry configuration information (e.g., a [=Sequence Header OBU=] or [=Layer Configuration Record OBU=]), metadata, or coded video data.

A Temporal Unit MAY contain multiple coded pictures but only one is output. AV2 defines a number of coded-frame OBU types, including [=Closed Loop Key OBUs=], [=Open Loop Key OBUs=], regular and leading tile-group OBUs, [=Switch OBUs=], <code>OBU_RAS_FRAME</code>, [=Bridge Frame OBUs=], and TIP (Temporally Interpolated Prediction) frames.

Frames that can be decoded without reference to other frames are [=Key Frames=] (carried in a [=Closed Loop Key OBU=] or an [=Open Loop Key OBU=]) and [=Intra frames=]. All other coded frames - including [=Inter Frames=], [=Switch Frames=], RAS frames, Bridge frames, TIP frames, and frames with [=show_existing_frame=] equal to 1 - have coding dependencies on other frames in the same or previous Temporal Units.

A [=Closed Random Access=] is the random access process that applies to an extended layer whose first coded frame is a [=Key Frame=] carried in a [=Closed Loop Key OBU=]. It starts a new coded video sequence for the extended layer; the layer's reference frame buffers are invalidated and every subsequent frame of that layer can be decoded. This is the primary random-access mechanism.

An [=Open Random Access=] is the random access process that applies to an extended layer whose first coded frame is a [=Key Frame=] carried in an [=Open Loop Key OBU=]. During sequential decoding, an [=Open Random Access=] point does not start a new coded video sequence; however, when a decoder initiates decoding at that point, the decoding process is treated as if it were the start of a new coded video sequence for the extended layer. [=Leading frames=] that follow an [=Open Random Access=] point MAY reference frames that precede it, and are discarded when decoding begins at the [=Open Random Access=] point.

In addition to Key Frames, AV2 provides two further mechanisms that support random access or stream switching: a RAS frame (<code>OBU_RAS_FRAME</code>) is an inter-predicted frame that uses long-term reference frames and enables random access or switching without inserting a full key frame; a [=Switch Frame=] (<code>OBU_SWITCH</code>) is an inter-predicted frame that enables switching between representations at a given point, typically in adaptive streaming scenarios.

AV2 supports three scalability dimensions: temporal layers (identified by [=obu_tlayer_id=]), embedded layers (identified by [=obu_mlayer_id=]), and extended layers (identified by [=obu_xlayer_id=]). The reserved [=obu_xlayer_id=] value <code>GLOBAL_XLAYER_ID</code> (equal to 31, as defined in [[!AV2]]) denotes global scope and is used by OBUs that do not belong to any specific extended layer (such as the [=Temporal Delimiter OBU=]). A bitstream that uses a single distinct non-global value of [=obu_xlayer_id=] is a [=Singlestream=] bitstream; a bitstream that uses two or more distinct non-global values is a [=Multistream=] bitstream.

AV2 defines two distinct [=Metadata OBU=] types for carrying metadata: <code>OBU_METADATA_SHORT</code>, using the [=metadata short OBU syntax=], and <code>OBU_METADATA_GROUP</code>, using the [=metadata group OBU syntax=]. A separate OBU type carries film grain synthesis parameters; its presence is indicated by the <code>film_grain_params_present</code> flag in the [=Sequence Header OBU=].

The [=Sequence Header OBU=] also carries the bitstream's profile, level, and - when applicable - tier, as defined in Annex A of [[!AV2]].

The [=Sequence Header OBU=] carries a <code>monotonic_output_order_flag</code> that defines the output mode of the associated coded video sequence.

When <code>monotonic_output_order_flag</code> is equal to 1, the output order of coded output frame equals their decoding order within the coded video sequence. Within a <l spec=ISOBMFF>[=sample=]</l>, the composition time (CTS) of the associated output frame is equal to the <l spec=ISOBMFF>[=sample=]</l>'s decoding time (DTS); the <l spec=ISOBMFF>[=sample=]</l> MAY additionally contain hidden frames.

When <code>monotonic_output_order_flag</code> is equal to 0, the output order of coded output frames MAY differ from their decoding order. The composition time of each <l spec=ISOBMFF>[=sample=]</l> is then derived from a 'ctts' box that signals the offset between the <l spec=ISOBMFF>[=sample=]</l>'s decoding time (DTS) and the composition time of its associated output frame. As in the monotonic case, a <l spec=ISOBMFF>[=sample=]</l> MAY additionally contain hidden frames.

NOTE: Non-monotonic output mode is new in AV2; AV1 supports only the monotonic mode.

# Basic Encapsulation Scheme # {#basic-encapsulation}

This section describes the basic data structures used to signal encapsulation of [=AV2 bitstreams=] in [[!ISOBMFF]] containers.

There are two locations where [=OBUs=] can be found in a file conformant to this specification:
- Some [=High-Level Syntax=] [=OBUs=], such as the [=Sequence Header OBU=], can be carried in an [=OutOfBandAV2CodecConfigurationBox=] as described in [[#sample-entry-and-config]]. This corresponds to "availability through external means" as described in the [[!AV2]] specification. These [=OBUs=] apply to all <l spec=ISOBMFF>[=samples=]</l> of the corresponding [=AV2SampleEntry=].
- The other [=OBUs=] are stored in <l spec=ISOBMFF>[=samples=]</l>. This corresponds to "presence in the bitstream" as described in the [[!AV2]] specification.

An <dfn>AV2 sample</dfn> is the union of a <l spec=ISOBMFF>[=sample=]</l> inclusive of the [=OBUs=] it carries, any [=OBUs=] carried in the [=AV2CodecConfigurationBox=] of the corresponding [=AV2SampleEntry=], and an implicit [=Temporal Delimiter OBU=].

NOTE: This specification refers to <l spec=ISOBMFF>[=samples=]</l> as defined in [[!ISOBMFF]], which are not to be mistaken with <l spec=AV2>[=samples=]</l> or [=sample values=] as defined in the [[!AV2]] specification.

## General Requirements & Brands ## {#general_requirements}

A file conformant to this specification satisfies the following:
- <assert>It SHALL conform to the normative requirements of [[!ISOBMFF]]</assert>
- <assert>It SHALL have the <dfn value export for="ISOBMFF Brand">av02</dfn> brand among the compatible brands array of the FileTypeBox</assert>
- <assert>It SHALL contain at least one track using an [=AV2SampleEntry=], possibly transformed by encryption as specified in [[#CommonEncryption]]</assert>
- <assert>It SHOULD indicate a structural ISOBMFF brand among the compatible brands array of the FileTypeBox, such as 'iso6'</assert>
- <assert>It SHALL contain at least one [=AV2 sample=]</assert>
- <assert>Each [=AV2 sample=] it contains SHALL form exactly one [[!AV2]] [=Temporal Unit=] if reconstructed as described in [[#av2-sample-reconstruction]]</assert>

## AV2 Sample Entry and Configuration ## {#sample-entry-and-config}

### AV2 Sample Entry ### {#av2-sample-entry}

The <dfn>AV2SampleEntry</dfn> extends [=VisualSampleEntry=] and signals a track carrying [=AV2 samples=]. There are two [=AV2SampleEntry=] flavours.

```cpp
abstract class AV2SampleEntry(int codingname) extends VisualSampleEntry(codingname) {
}

class OutOfBandAV2SampleEntry extends AV2SampleEntry('av2E') {
    OutOfBandAV2CodecConfigurationBox config;
}

class InBandAV2SampleEntry extends AV2SampleEntry('av2e') {
    InBandAV2CodecConfigurationBox config;
}
```

<p>An <dfn>OutOfBandAV2SampleEntry</dfn> contains an [=OutOfBandAV2CodecConfigurationBox=] and an <dfn>InBandAV2SampleEntry</dfn> contains an [=InBandAV2CodecConfigurationBox=].</p>

<p><assert>An [=InBandAV2SampleEntry=] MAY be used instead of an [=OutOfBandAV2SampleEntry=], if the content of an [=OBU=] of a type that may be carried by an [=OutOfBandAV2CodecConfigurationBox=] changes during the sequence, and if that sequence cannot be split into multiple [=OutOfBandAV2SampleEntries=]. Otherwise, an [=OutOfBandAV2SampleEntry=] SHOULD be used.</assert></p>

<p>An <dfn>OutOfBandAV2SampleEntry</dfn> contains an [=OutOfBandAV2CodecConfigurationBox=] and an <dfn>InBandAV2SampleEntry</dfn> contains an [=InBandAV2CodecConfigurationBox=].</p>

<p><assert>An [=InBandAV2SampleEntry=] MAY be used instead of an [=OutOfBandAV2SampleEntry=], if the content of an [=OBU=] of a type that may be carried by an [=OutOfBandAV2CodecConfigurationBox=] changes during the sequence, and if that sequence cannot be split into multiple [=OutOfBandAV2SampleEntries=]. Otherwise, an [=OutOfBandAV2SampleEntry=] SHOULD be used.</assert></p>

<p><assert>An [=AV2SampleEntry=] SHALL contain exactly one [=AV2CodecConfigurationBox=].</assert> <assert>Each [=layer=] in an [=AV2SampleEntry=] SHALL be described by exactly one [=AV2CodecConfigurationBox=].</assert></p>

<p><assert>Unless explicitly stated otherwise in the definition of a box, the direct child boxes of an [=AV2SampleEntry=] describe all [=base layers=] in that [=AV2SampleEntry=].</assert></p>

<assert>Each [=base layer=] in an [=AV2SampleEntry=] SHALL be described by exactly one 'colr' box with the 'nclx' 'colour_type'.</assert> Each value among <code>colour_primaries</code>, <code>transfer_characteristics</code>, and <code>matrix_coefficients</code> carried in that 'colr' box, for the [=layers=] or operating points it applies to:
- <assert>SHOULD equal the corresponding effective value of the [=AV2 bitstream=] carried by the track if the latter is anything but 2 (<code>Unspecified</code>)</assert>;
- <assert>SHALL take precedence over the corresponding effective value of the [=AV2 bitstream=] carried by the track</assert>.

<p><assert>The value of <code>full_range_flag</code> carried in that 'colr' box, for the [=layers=] or operating points it applies to, SHOULD equal the corresponding effective value of the [=AV2 bitstream=] carried by the track and SHALL take precedence over the corresponding effective value of the [=AV2 bitstream=] carried by the track.</assert></p>

<p><assert>Each [=base layer=] in an [=AV2SampleEntry=] SHALL be described by exactly one 'pixi' box.</assert> <assert>'pixi' boxes in an [=AV2SampleEntry=] SHALL have the least significant bit of 'px_flags' enabled.</assert> The constraints described in [[#layers]] apply to that [=AV2SampleEntry=].</p>

NOTE: An [=AV2SampleEntry=] may contain additional direct child boxes permitted by [[!ISOBMFF]] for a [=VisualSampleEntry=], such as 'colr' with a 'colour_type' value other than 'nclx', 'pasp', 'clli', 'mdcv' or 'btrt'. They may be located before and/or after the [=AV2CodecConfigurationBox=].

NOTE: An [=AV2SampleEntry=] may contain additional boxes, for example 'colr' when carried by the <code>LayerPropertyContainerBox</code> as defined in the draft of ISOBMFF 14496-12 10th Edition to describe the colour properties of [=enhancement layers=].

### AV2 Codec Configuration Box ### {#av2c}

The <dfn>AV2CodecConfigurationBox</dfn> carries the decoder initialisation data required to decode the [=AV2 samples=] of a track. There are two [=AV2CodecConfigurationBox=] flavours.

An [=AV2CodecConfigurationBox=] that is the direct child box of an [=AV2SampleEntry=] describes all [=layers=] in that [=AV2SampleEntry=].

#### Description

<p><assert>An [=OutOfBandAV2CodecConfigurationBox=] MAY carry [=OBUs=] of the following types: <code>OBU_MSDO</code>, <code>OBU_LAYER_CONFIGURATION_RECORD</code>, <code>OBU_OPERATING_POINT_SET</code>, <code>OBU_ATLAS_SEGMENT</code>, <code>OBU_METADATA_SHORT</code> with <code>obu_xlayer_id equal</code> equal to <code>GLOBAL_XLAYER_ID</code> and <code>metadata_is_suffix</code> equal to 0, <code>OBU_METADATA_GROUP</code> with <code>metadata_is_suffix</code>=0, and <code>OBU_SEQUENCE_HEADER</code>.</assert></p>

<p><assert>An [=OutOfBandAV2CodecConfigurationBox=] SHALL NOT carry [=OBUs=] of the following types: <code>OBU_TEMPORAL_DELIMITER</code>, <code>OBU_CONTENT_INTERPRETATION</code>, <code>OBU_MULTI_FRAME_HEADER</code>, <code>OBU_BUFFER_REMOVAL_TIMING</code>, <code>OBU_QUANTIZATION_MATRIX</code>, <code>OBU_FILM_GRAIN</code>, <code>OBU_CLOSED_LOOP_KEY</code>, <code>OBU_OPEN_LOOP_KEY</code>, <code>OBU_LEADING_TILE_GROUP</code>, <code>OBU_REGULAR_TILE_GROUP</code>, <code>OBU_SWITCH</code>, <code>OBU_LEADING_TIP</code>, <code>OBU_REGULAR_TIP</code>, <code>OBU_BRIDGE_FRAME</code>, <code>OBU_RAS_FRAME</code>, <code>OBU_METADATA_SHORT</code> with <code>obu_xlayer_id equal</code> not equal to <code>GLOBAL_XLAYER_ID</code> or <code>metadata_is_suffix</code> equal to 1, <code>OBU_METADATA_GROUP</code> with <code>obu_xlayer_id equal</code> not equal to <code>GLOBAL_XLAYER_ID</code> or <code>metadata_is_suffix</code> equal to 1, and <code>OBU_PADDING</code>.</assert></p>

<p><assert>There SHOULD NOT be any [=Metadata OBU=] carried by an [=OutOfBandAV2CodecConfigurationBox=] if a codec-agnostic carriage solution exists for that metadata.</assert></p>

<p><assert>The [=OBUs=] carried by an [=OutOfBandAV2CodecConfigurationBox=] SHALL appear in the order specified by the [=ordering of OBUs in a temporal unit=] in [[!AV2]], with the [=grouped high level syntax block=] being present.</assert></p>

#### Syntax

```cpp
abstract class AV2CodecConfigurationBox(int codingname) extends Box(codingname)
{
}

aligned(8) class OutOfBandAV2CodecConfigurationBox extends AV2CodecConfigurationBox('av2C')
{
  unsigned int(8) reserved1 = 0;
  unsigned int(8) config_obus_count_minus1;
  for (i = 0; i < config_obus_count_minus1 + 1; ++i) {
    unsigned int(8) config_obu[];
  }
}

aligned(8) class InBandAV2CodecConfigurationBox extends AV2CodecConfigurationBox('av2c')
{
  unsigned int(3) reserved1 = 0;
  unsigned int(2) max_num_streams_minus_1;
  unsigned int(5) max_profile_idc;
  unsigned int(5) max_level_idx;
  unsigned int(1) max_tier;
}
```

<p class="issue">Editor's note: The exact fields to carry in InBandAV2CodecConfigurationBox should be studied further.</p>

#### Semantics

<p><assert><code>reserved1</code> SHALL be set to 0. Readers SHALL ignore its value.</assert></p>

<p class="issue">Editor's note: Should reserved1 be renamed to reserved?</p>

<code>config_obus_count_minus1</code> is the number of <code>config_obu</code> minus one.

<code>config_obu</code> is a byte array. <assert>Each <code>config_obu</code> SHALL carry a single OBU preceded by a <code>leb128()</code> <code>num_bytes_in_obu</code> value giving the byte length of that OBU, as specified in the [=Length delimited bitstream format=] from Annex B of [[!AV2]].</assert>

<code>max_num_streams_minus_1</code> specifies the maximum number of independent streams in the bitstream.
- <assert>There SHALL NOT be any [=Multi Stream Decoder Operation OBU=] in the corresponding [=AV2 sample=] whose <code>num_streams_minus_2</code> value is greater than or equal to <code>max_num_streams_minus_1</code>.</assert>
- <assert>If <code>max_num_streams_minus_1</code> is not zero, there SHOULD be at least one [=Multi Stream Decoder Operation OBU=] in the corresponding [=AV2 sample=].</assert>

NOTE: The above means there shall be no [=Multi Stream Decoder Operation OBU=] if <code>max_num_streams_minus_1</code> is set to 0.

NOTE: It is a requirement of bitstream conformance that <code>num_streams_minus_2</code> is not greater than 2 in [[!AV2]], so <code>max_num_streams_minus_1</code> fits in two bits. <code>reserved1</code> can be repurposed once <code>num_streams_minus_2</code> uses its three allocated bits in a future version of [[!AV2]].

<code>max_profile_idc</code> specifies the maximum profile for the coded video sequence.
- <assert>There SHALL NOT be any [=Sequence Header OBU=] in the corresponding [=AV2 sample=] whose <code>seq_profile_idc</code> value is greater than <code>max_profile_idc</code>.</assert>
- <assert>There SHALL NOT be any [=Multi Stream Decoder Operation OBU=] in the corresponding [=AV2 sample=] whose <code>multistream_profile_idc</code> value is greater than <code>max_profile_idc</code>.</assert>
- <assert>There SHOULD be at least one [=Sequence Header OBU=] in the corresponding [=AV2 sample=] whose <code>seq_profile_idc</code> has the same value as <code>max_profile_idc</code>, or at least one [=Multi Stream Decoder Operation OBU=] in the corresponding [=AV2 sample=] whose <code>multistream_profile_idc</code> has the same value as <code>max_profile_idc</code>.</assert>

<code>max_level_idx</code> specifies the maximum level that the coded video sequence conforms to.
- <assert>There SHALL NOT be any [=Sequence Header OBU=] in the corresponding [=AV2 sample=] whose <code>seq_level_idx</code> value is greater than <code>max_level_idx</code>.</assert>
- <assert>There SHALL NOT be any [=Multi Stream Decoder Operation OBU=] in the corresponding [=AV2 sample=] whose <code>multistream_level_idx</code> value is greater than <code>max_level_idx</code>.</assert>
- <assert>There SHOULD be at least one [=Sequence Header OBU=] in the corresponding [=AV2 sample=] whose <code>seq_level_idx</code> has the same value as <code>max_level_idx</code>, or at least one [=Multi Stream Decoder Operation OBU=] in the corresponding [=AV2 sample=] whose <code>multistream_level_idx</code> has the same value as <code>max_level_idx</code>.</assert>

<code>max_tier</code> specifies the maximum tier that the coded video sequence conforms to.
- <assert>There SHALL NOT be any [=Sequence Header OBU=] in the corresponding [=AV2 sample=] whose <code>seq_tier</code> value is greater than <code>max_tier</code>.</assert>
- <assert>There SHALL NOT be any [=Multi Stream Decoder Operation OBU=] in the corresponding [=AV2 sample=] whose <code>multistream_tier</code> value is greater than <code>max_tier</code>.</assert>
- <assert>There SHOULD be at least one [=Sequence Header OBU=] in the corresponding [=AV2 sample=] whose <code>seq_tier</code> has the same value as <code>max_tier</code>, or at least one [=Multi Stream Decoder Operation OBU=] in the corresponding [=AV2 sample=] whose <code>multistream_tier</code> has the same value as <code>max_tier</code>.</assert>


<p class="issue">Editor's note: for a [=Multistream=] bitstream, the [=AV2CodecConfigurationBox=] contains a [=Sequence Header OBU=] for each extended layer. The impact on multi-layer use cases — including how a reader determines the active decoder configuration per extended layer from multiple Sequence Header OBUs — needs investigation. Also how profile / level is signalled to decoder API for layers. etc.</p>

## AV2 Sample Format ## {#sample-format}

### General ### {#sample-format-general}

The [=AV2 sample=] boundary delimits the temporal unit.

<p><assert>Each [=OBU=] within a <l spec=ISOBMFF>[=sample=]</l> SHALL be framed using the [=Length delimited bitstream format=] specified in Annex B of [[!AV2]]: each OBU is preceded by a <code>leb128()</code> <code>num_bytes_in_obu</code> field giving the byte length of the OBU that follows.</assert> <a class="figure-ref" href="#figure-sample-tu-mapping">Figure</a> illustrates this mapping.</p>

<figure id="figure-sample-tu-mapping">
  <img src="images/av2_sample_tu_mapping.svg" alt="Mapping of AV2 temporal units to ISOBMFF track samples" width="800" height="420">
  <figcaption>Example mapping of AV2 temporal units into the ISOBMFF sample format.</figcaption>
</figure>

### OBUs in samples ### {#sample-obus}

The following applies to a <l spec=ISOBMFF>[=sample=]</l> associated with an [=AV2SampleEntry=]:
- <assert>The [=OBUs=] carried by a <l spec=ISOBMFF>[=sample=]</l> SHALL appear in the order specified by the [=ordering of OBUs in a temporal unit=] in [[!AV2]].</assert>
- <assert>The <l spec=ISOBMFF>[=sample=]</l> SHALL NOT carry an [=OBU=] of a type among <code>OBU_TEMPORAL_DELIMITER</code>, <code>OBU_CONTENT_INTERPRETATION</code> and <code>OBU_PADDING</code>.</assert>

    NOTE: The [=AV2 sample=] boundary already delimits the temporal unit, and byte-level padding within a track is achieved using ISOBMFF mechanisms, e.g. 'free'/'skip' boxes or <l spec=ISOBMFF>[=sample=]</l> size signalling.

- <assert>There SHOULD NOT be any [=Metadata OBU=] carried by a <l spec=ISOBMFF>[=sample=]</l> if a container-level carriage solution exists for that metadata.</assert>

The following applies to a <l spec=ISOBMFF>[=sample=]</l> associated with an [=AV2SampleEntry=] containing an [=OutOfBandAV2CodecConfigurationBox=]:
- <assert>The <l spec=ISOBMFF>[=sample=]</l> SHALL NOT carry an [=OBU=] of a type among the types allowed to be carried in an [=OutOfBandAV2CodecConfigurationBox=] as listed in [[#av2c]], unless there is a bit-exact copy of that [=OBU=] (type and content) in the associated [=OutOfBandAV2CodecConfigurationBox=].</assert>
- <assert>The [=OBUs=] present in both the <l spec=ISOBMFF>[=sample=]</l> and the associated [=OutOfBandAV2CodecConfigurationBox=], identified by the same type and content, SHALL be present in the same order.</assert>
- <assert>A decoder implementation MAY skip, in the <l spec=ISOBMFF>[=sample=]</l>, any [=OBU=] of a type among the types of the [=OBUs=] carried in the associated [=OutOfBandAV2CodecConfigurationBox=].</assert>

    <p class="issue">Editor's note: Double-check that OBU skipping leads to the same output in all cases. Otherwise another assertion would be needed: "The sample SHALL contain all necessary OBUs so that any OBU skipped this way by a decoder implementation leads to the same output as if the OBU was not skipped".</p>

- <assert>The <l spec=ISOBMFF>[=sample=]</l> SHOULD NOT carry an [=OBU=] of a type among the types allowed to be carried in an [=OutOfBandAV2CodecConfigurationBox=].</assert>

    <p class="issue">Editor's note: Is this fine to advise against OBU repetitions? Can HLS OBUs be forbidden entirely in samples when an [=OutOfBandAV2CodecConfigurationBox=] is present?</p>

### Content Interpretation OBU

The following container-level signalling is available to replace the semantics of the following [=Content Interpretation OBU=] fields:
- <code>ci_scan_type_idc</code>: 'ilce' sample group from ISO/IEC [[!23001-17]]
- <code>ci_color_description_idc</code>, <code>ci_color_primaries</code>, <code>ci_transfer_characteristics</code>, <code>ci_matrix_coefficients</code>, and <code>ci_full_range_flag</code>: 'colr' box from [[!ISOBMFF]] with the 'nclx' 'colour_type'
- <code>ci_chroma_sample_position_top</code>: 'pixi' box from [[!ISOBMFF]]
- <code>ci_aspect_ratio_idc</code>, <code>ci_sar_width</code>, and <code>ci_sar_height</code>: 'iso3' brand, 'pasr' sample group, or 'pasp' box from [[!ISOBMFF]]
- <code>timing_info()</code>: 'mvhd' and 'stts' boxes from [[!ISOBMFF]]

### Sync sample ### {#sync-sample}

<p>An [=AV2 sample=] is a <dfn>sync AV2 sample</dfn> if, for every [=coded extended layer unit=] present in the [=AV2 sample=], the first coded frame OBU of that coded extended layer unit has <code>obu_type</code> equal to <code>OBU_CLOSED_LOOP_KEY</code>. Such an [=AV2 sample=] is a [=Closed Random Access=] point for the carried bitstream and corresponds to a SAP of type 1 or 2 as defined in Annex I of [[!ISOBMFF]].</p>

<p><assert>A [=sync AV2 sample=] SHALL be self-sufficient for starting decoding at that point for all layers: every OBU referenced by the coded frame OBUs of the [=sync AV2 sample=] SHALL be available either by being carried in the [=AV2CodecConfigurationBox=] of the active [=AV2SampleEntry=] or by being present in the <l spec=ISOBMFF>[=sample=]</l>, as required by the [=availability of HLS OBUs=] in [[!AV2]].</assert></p>

NOTE: In ISOBMFF terms, sync samples are signalled using the SyncSampleBox ('stss') in unfragmented tracks, or by setting <code>sample_is_non_sync_sample</code> equal to 0 in fragmented tracks. When every sample in a track is a sync sample, the SyncSampleBox is omitted in unfragmented tracks (per [[!ISOBMFF]]), and in fragmented tracks this is expressed through the default sample flags of the MovieExtendsBox ('trex') or TrackFragmentHeaderBox ('tfhd') with no per-sample override.

### Layers ### {#layers}

In an [=AV2 sample=], the following applies to all extended and embedded layers of each temporal layer associated with a 'pixi' box:
- The channel at index <code>i</code> in the 'pixi' box corresponds to the (<code>i</code>+1)th channel among the extended and embedded layers associated with the 'pixi' box. This is the case for each <code>tlayer_id</code> unique value.
- The channels in the [=AV2 sample=] associated with that 'pixi' box are considered to be ordered as if the extended and embedded layers were concatenated in increasing <code>xlayer_id</code> order, then in increasing <code>mlayer_id</code> order.
- <assert>If the 'pixi' box describes a channel as used and specified (<code>channel_idc</code> values other than 0 and 1), the corresponding channel in the [=AV2 sample=] SHALL be present.</assert>
- <assert>If the 'pixi' box describes a channel to be a color channel (<code>channel_idc</code> values such as 2, 3, 4, and 7), the corresponding channel in the [=AV2 sample=] SHALL be a color channel: if signalled, the <code>lcr_layer_type</code> field of its associated [=Layer Configuration Record OBU=] SHALL be set to 0 (<code>TEXTURE_LAYER</code>).</assert>
- <assert>If the 'pixi' box describes a channel to be an alpha channel (<code>channel_idc</code> 5), the corresponding channel in the [=AV2 sample=] SHALL be an alpha channel: if signalled, the <code>lcr_layer_type</code> field of its associated [=Layer Configuration Record OBU=] SHALL be set to 1 (<code>AUX_LAYER</code>) and <code>lcr_auxiliary_type</code> to 0 (<code>ALPHA_AUX</code>).</assert>
- <assert>If the 'pixi' box describes a channel to be a depth channel (<code>channel_idc</code> 6), the corresponding channel in the [=AV2 sample=] SHALL be a depth channel: if signalled, the <code>lcr_layer_type</code> field of its associated [=Layer Configuration Record OBU=] SHALL be set to 1 (<code>AUX_LAYER</code>) and <code>lcr_auxiliary_type</code> to 1 (<code>DEPTH_AUX</code>).</assert>
- <assert>If the 'pixi' box describes a channel as used and specified (<code>channel_idc</code> values other than 0 and 1) with <code>subsampling_flag</code> set to 1, the corresponding channel in the [=AV2 sample=] SHALL have the value of the <code>chroma_format_idc</code> field of its associated [=Sequence Header OBU=] correspond to the same meaning as the value of the 'pixi' box's corresponding channel's <code>subsampling_type</code> value.</assert>

